# Line endings.
#
# `*.rs` matters because rustc rejects a bare CR inside a doc-comment
# ("error: bare CR not allowed in doc-comment"). 18 tracked Rust files were
# committed with CRLF, so checking out this repo on Linux — which CI does, and
# so does any builder — fails to compile economy-service, admin-service and
# others. Normalising .rs (and the other text types the toolchain parses) to LF
# makes the checkout reproducible regardless of the contributor's platform.
#
# Normalising with `git add --renormalize .` re-stages the existing blobs; a
# checkout on its own does not rewrite history.
*.rs   text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.sql  text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf

# Shell checks run on Linux in CI; retain LF locally as well.
*.sh   text eol=lf

# Never rewrite these: they are binary, and a blanket text rule would corrupt
# them or make git diff them as text.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
*.tgz   binary
*.wasm  binary
*.so    binary
*.dll   binary
*.exe   binary
